In article <BxxtCr.KEC@cs.columbia.edu> vh@cs.columbia.edu (Vasileios Hatzivassiloglou) writes:
>>Stormbringer makes no difference in what intrinsics you can get.
>Stormbringer makes a big difference in how easy you get the intrinsics. Each
>time that you hit a monster with Stormbringer, it loses one level. When you
>eat the corpse it leaves, your chance of getting any specific intrinsic is
>(monster level)/(some constant depending on the intrinsic). Therefore, hitting
>5 times a red dragon with Stormbringer, lowers your chances for getting fire
>resistance from 2/3 to 1/3 (for example), and the effect is more important for
>lower level monsters (e.g. try to get teleport control by killing tengus with
>Stormy).

The percentage chance of intrinsics depends on the monster's typical level,
not on the level of the specific corpse you happened to kill.

Teleport control is hard to get that way because teleport control from tengus
is hard to get, period.
